# =============================================================================
# Preserve bytes exactly as committed.
#
# This repository's claim is that every script is byte-identical to the working
# tree that produced the manuscript, verified by reversing the path
# substitution and comparing raw bytes. Git's default end-of-line normalisation
# would break that claim at checkout: `core.autocrlf=true` stores blobs as LF
# and converts back to CRLF on Windows, which silently rewrites the 16 mixed
# bare-LF lines that several of these files genuinely contain.
#
# `-text` disables that conversion in both directions, so a clone reproduces
# the committed bytes on every platform. Mixed line endings inside a file are
# preserved because they are part of what was verified, not an accident to be
# tidied.
# =============================================================================

* -text
